{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 56, :comments ["<b>And Yosef opened all.</b> The reason he opened all the storehouses and did not suffice with what was needed: he intended to inspect them all, to know what he should sell first and what he could hold back longer without spoiling." "<b>Further,</b> since the produce of the fields of a city [which] (he placed) in its surroundings [he placed within it], therefore he acted wisely and opened all the storehouses in each and every place, so that each and every city would rely on what is right before it — and one who has bread in his basket is not comparable [to one who must fetch it from afar]. Also, they would not need to exert themselves to bring everything from one place." "Also, perhaps he intended to open them all so that when the people of the city see the great abundance they would not feel hunger — for hunger enters a person's heart when he sees there is a shortage, and when they see all the storehouses opened, the burning heat of the famine in their hearts would cool. Yet even so, the verse informs: ״וַיֶּחֱזַק הָרָעָב״ — and it availed them nothing, on account of the intensity of the famine."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {1 "The Hebrew bracketed text contains variant readings; translated hyper-literally as transmitted."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:52.598899369Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}